{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>A great voice, and it did not cease.</b> That is, it did not cease; and so Onkelos, of blessed memory, translated. And you will find here seven voices: the first, ״קול גדול״; the second, ״ויהי כשמעכם את הקול״; the third, ״ואת קולו שמענו״; the fourth, ״אם יוספים אנחנו לשמוע את קול HaShem Eloheinu״; the fifth, ״כי מי כל בשר אשר שמע קול״; the sixth, ״וישמע HaShem את קול״; the seventh, ״שמעתי את קול דברי העם״. And this is what the Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded: 'The Torah was given in seven voices.' And likewise seven voices are mentioned in the first Decalogue, and I have already cited them there."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:45:52.676190056Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}